WEBVTT

00:03.900 --> 00:09.530
In other words, Rome and Carthage fought three times over the years.

00:10.500 --> 00:12.470
In the Second Punic War,

00:12.570 --> 00:15.940
Carthage's hero Hannibal took the field, but...

00:15.640 --> 00:16.770
Good morning.

00:17.410 --> 00:21.110
Don't "good morning" me!
What time do you think it is?!

00:21.610 --> 00:24.340
This is the 6th time since the start of the second semester!

00:24.650 --> 00:25.640
Get your act together!

00:27.090 --> 00:28.080
I'm sorry.

00:30.420 --> 00:32.090
Oh, fine. Take your seat!

00:32.090 --> 00:33.320
Yes, Sir.

00:47.640 --> 00:50.170
Let's see, where was I?

00:52.010 --> 00:55.570
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

00:56.080 --> 00:59.220
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

00:59.220 --> 01:02.780
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

01:03.020 --> 01:06.050
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

01:06.320 --> 01:09.960
<i>It just doesn't get across...</i>
<i>Nani o Shite mo Tsutawarazu</i>

01:09.960 --> 01:13.530
<i>It's just not working right at all.</i>
<i>Umaku Ikanai Bakari de</i>

01:13.530 --> 01:16.900
<i>But even I and everyone else...</i>
<i>Watashi Datte Dare Datte</i>

01:17.100 --> 01:20.600
<i>... have times like that.</i>
<i>Atarimae ni Aru Koto</i>

01:20.710 --> 01:24.070
<i>Those things that don't return to your heart.</i>
<i>Mune no Naka ni Kaeranai</i>

01:24.280 --> 01:27.680
<i>But even those words and feelings...</i>
<i>Omoi mo Kotoba mo Itsuka</i>

01:27.850 --> 01:32.250
<i>... will come back in time someday...</i>
<i>Jikan ga Tateba Modotte Kuru kara</i>

01:32.480 --> 01:35.390
<i>... before you know it.</i>
<i>Shiranai Uchi ni</i>

01:35.690 --> 01:41.630
<i>There's only one thing you can do right now.</i>
<i>Ima Kimiga Dekiru Koto wa Hitotsu</i>

01:41.960 --> 01:48.700
<i>Just accept it and go with it.</i>
<i>Sono Mama Ukeirete Yukou</i>

01:49.330 --> 01:53.290
<i>Just be you and stay true to yourself.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Itsuwarazu ni</i>

01:53.370 --> 01:56.510
<i>Take a little break.</i>
<i>Sukoshi Hitoyasumi Shite</i>

01:56.510 --> 02:00.280
<i>Take your impatience and your hardships...</i>
<i>Aseru Kimochi Kurushii Koto</i>

02:00.280 --> 02:03.540
<i>...and turn them into your strengths.</i>
<i>Kimi no Power ni Kaete</i>

02:03.620 --> 02:07.380
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

02:07.720 --> 02:10.860
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

02:10.860 --> 02:14.450
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

02:14.630 --> 02:17.560
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

02:20.570 --> 02:27.340
<i>THE UNFORGETTABLE</i>

02:20.570 --> 02:27.340
<i>DREAM</i>

02:30.880 --> 02:32.040
Hey, hey, Mizuki.

02:32.110 --> 02:33.340
Are you free today?

02:33.340 --> 02:35.040
I don't really have anything going on...

02:35.150 --> 02:37.210
Then, you wanna go eat crepes together?

02:37.380 --> 02:39.110
We found a really good place!

02:42.120 --> 02:44.180
Hasn't Sendou been acting a little strange lately?

02:44.320 --> 02:46.290
He's been tardy a lot and not very energetic.

02:46.760 --> 02:48.950
I wonder if something happened during summer break?

02:49.530 --> 02:50.790
Mizuki, do you know anything?

02:52.260 --> 02:53.230
Beats me.

02:54.100 --> 02:55.330
What?!

02:56.070 --> 02:58.940
What did you just say, Comrade Kazuki?

02:59.570 --> 03:03.470
Once more! Let's hear it one more time!

03:04.410 --> 03:07.280
I said, I'm gonna quit doujin work.

03:09.780 --> 03:11.550
Very funny, my brother!

03:11.550 --> 03:14.310
A funny story, very similar to an American joke!

03:17.290 --> 03:19.280
Here's the project plan for the winter Comi-Pa.

03:19.660 --> 03:22.290
I call it, "For Comi-Pa Part One"!

03:22.930 --> 03:23.990
If you execute this plan,

03:24.060 --> 03:27.190
we will undoubtedly be one step closer to conquering the world!

03:27.730 --> 03:29.360
What is wrong, my brother?

03:29.770 --> 03:31.240
Come, take it.

03:33.000 --> 03:34.030
Comi-Pa, huh?

03:34.610 --> 03:36.540
Well, just do your best.

03:36.910 --> 03:37.840
No!

03:38.680 --> 03:40.510
This has to do with you, my brother!

03:40.980 --> 03:42.280
I believe I told you this before.

03:42.380 --> 03:45.010
The failure at the summer
Comi-Pa does not count!

03:45.750 --> 03:47.690
Use this as your fuel and your stepping-stone...

03:47.790 --> 03:50.410
...to charge on towards world conquest!

03:51.620 --> 03:52.780
My brother?

03:53.160 --> 03:54.590
I don't understand anymore.

03:54.760 --> 03:57.460
What was I drawing doujinshi for, anyway?

04:08.040 --> 04:11.130
Doujin work. It is an endless giant mountain range,

04:11.310 --> 04:14.340
an enormously vast ocean, the profoundly colossal universe!

04:14.710 --> 04:17.840
It is a world where everyone will become lost, at one point in time or another.

04:20.020 --> 04:21.850
Endure the trials!

04:22.120 --> 04:23.760
Overcome this life-or-death crisis!

04:23.760 --> 04:27.620
And come back to life as the phoenix did!

04:28.360 --> 04:31.630
Comrade Kazuki!

04:46.340 --> 04:48.610
Well well, you sure cleaned things up.

04:49.010 --> 04:49.710
Yuu?

04:49.710 --> 04:52.620
I heard from Taishi that you're gonna quit doujin work.

04:53.350 --> 04:54.980
It's no use trying to convince me otherwise.

04:55.520 --> 04:57.490
I'm not gonna do that.

04:57.560 --> 04:59.550
You do doujin work 'cause you like doin' it.

04:59.720 --> 05:01.920
Whether you quit or continue is up to you.

05:02.230 --> 05:04.320
It's not my place to interfere.

05:04.760 --> 05:06.700
Then what do you want?

05:07.370 --> 05:09.960
Well, that's quite a welcome.

05:10.600 --> 05:13.500
I just want you to keep me company for the next festival.

05:13.640 --> 05:15.000
Keep you company?

05:15.140 --> 05:16.270
Yup!

05:18.310 --> 05:20.880
COMIC WASSHOI

05:18.980 --> 05:20.410
An exhibition and spot sale?

05:21.910 --> 05:22.970
I'm countin' on you to be a shopboy.

05:23.620 --> 05:25.880
A shopboy? But I'm already...

05:26.550 --> 05:29.990
I'm short-handed and desperate for any help I can get.

05:30.220 --> 05:32.350
Besides, you owe me, right?

05:32.790 --> 05:33.660
What?

05:33.660 --> 05:36.250
The traditions of an exhibition and spot sale.

05:36.360 --> 05:39.590
How to make a doujinshi.
Negotiating with the printshops.

05:39.800 --> 05:42.530
I taught you the ABCs of doujin work.

05:42.670 --> 05:44.400
You're not gonna tell me you forgot!

05:45.040 --> 05:46.100
But...

05:46.100 --> 05:47.900
"It is a foul bird that fouls its own nest."

05:48.170 --> 05:53.130
If you're gonna quit doujin work, set the record straight before you do!

05:53.480 --> 05:55.950
That's what's called the honor among doujin!

05:56.310 --> 05:58.220
Well, but, that is...

05:58.650 --> 06:00.140
So, I'm countin' on ya!

06:00.690 --> 06:02.220
W-wait!

06:01.820 --> 06:03.210
There we go.

06:03.320 --> 06:04.480
Later!

06:12.730 --> 06:13.930
Yo, Mizuki!

06:15.370 --> 06:16.530
Miss Inagawa...

06:16.770 --> 06:18.430
Autumn sure is here.

06:18.570 --> 06:22.270
The mornings and nights have gotten real cool lately.

06:22.510 --> 06:24.310
What? Yes...

06:25.380 --> 06:27.370
So, how are things goin' these days?

06:27.880 --> 06:29.370
How? What do you mean?

06:29.550 --> 06:32.070
What do you think?
I'm talkin' about Kazuki.

06:33.750 --> 06:35.380
You don't have to play dumb with me.

06:35.520 --> 06:38.420
You two've been actin' a tad bit strange lately.

06:38.560 --> 06:39.850
Am I right?

06:41.690 --> 06:45.600
He doesn't talk at all, and he's gotten oddly standoffish.

06:45.930 --> 06:47.630
So, what about it?

06:50.500 --> 06:51.430
Because...

06:51.500 --> 06:54.840
Because I'm not Kazuki's girlfriend, or anything.

06:56.870 --> 06:58.900
There'll be no problem then.

06:59.680 --> 07:02.550
I asked Kazuki to be a shopboy for my group...

07:02.680 --> 07:04.980
...at the next exhibition and spot sale.

07:05.550 --> 07:08.280
Wh-what does that have to do with me?

07:08.820 --> 07:11.520
Well, nothin', I guess.

07:11.920 --> 07:15.220
But I thought I should get your okay on it.

07:16.230 --> 07:17.630
Go right ahead! Feel free!

07:17.700 --> 07:20.360
I couldn't care less what Kazuki does!

07:21.100 --> 07:23.160
I'm glad to hear it!

07:23.500 --> 07:25.940
Well, see you tomorrow at school!

07:30.980 --> 07:32.710
What should I do?

07:33.510 --> 07:36.380
In the end, I should repay my debts, right?

07:37.050 --> 07:39.680
But I've quit doujin work.

07:39.880 --> 07:41.750
Like hell I'll go to another exhibition and spot sale.

07:42.220 --> 07:45.160
That's right, I'm not going!

07:46.390 --> 07:48.160
There's no way I'll go!

07:58.400 --> 08:01.700
Hey! Don't just stand there! Give me a hand!

08:02.540 --> 08:03.910
Right...

08:05.480 --> 08:08.500
What're ya doin'?! It's precious product! Be careful!

08:08.580 --> 08:09.840
S-sorry!

08:16.320 --> 08:17.980
I'm sorry for having made a mess.

08:19.660 --> 08:21.790
Miss Aya! Are you assigned to this space?

08:22.160 --> 08:23.390
Oh, yes.

08:23.660 --> 08:25.290
Hey, you're the one...

08:26.060 --> 08:27.400
I'm Aya Hasebe.

08:27.500 --> 08:29.470
Come to think of it,
I never introduced myself.

08:29.530 --> 08:32.500
I'm Yuu Inagawa of
Karamitei. Nice to meet you.

08:32.870 --> 08:35.810
Must be some kind of fate that made us neighbors today.

08:35.910 --> 08:37.410
How about we sell together?

08:36.840 --> 08:37.880
What?

08:37.410 --> 08:40.870
We can go eat in shifts. It'll be convenient in all sorts of ways.

08:40.980 --> 08:42.710
So, let's do that.

08:43.610 --> 08:44.510
All right.

08:44.850 --> 08:47.280
Now that that's decided, let's get down to it!

08:49.090 --> 08:50.280
Come on, come on, gimme a hand!

08:51.060 --> 08:52.150
Right.

08:54.630 --> 08:57.490
Karamitei

08:54.930 --> 08:57.490
We've ended up with a joint space without even plannin' for it.

08:58.160 --> 08:59.630
Joint space?

09:00.200 --> 09:02.770
That's what you get when two friends request...

09:02.770 --> 09:04.830
...to have their spaces together.

09:08.670 --> 09:12.440
<i>Comic Wasshoi will now be open.</i>

09:20.590 --> 09:23.750
Karamitei

09:21.320 --> 09:23.750
It looks like there aren't that many people here today.

09:24.560 --> 09:28.150
Can't be helped.
It's like a late bargain sale.

09:29.590 --> 09:31.320
Part of exhibition and spot sales during this time of year...

09:31.430 --> 09:33.590
...tend to be for gettin' rid of leftover product.

09:33.830 --> 09:36.530
No one wants useless leftovers with winter comin'.

09:37.670 --> 09:39.860
You can just be laid back at times like this.

09:40.340 --> 09:42.330
I'm gonna go get somethin' to drink.

09:44.980 --> 09:46.540
<i>Getting rid of leftover product, huh?</i>

09:46.680 --> 09:48.410
<i>It's got nothing to do with me.</i>

09:48.480 --> 09:49.450
Um...

09:50.820 --> 09:52.080
Excuse me.

09:53.020 --> 09:53.880
I'd like this one.

09:54.220 --> 09:56.190
Oh, okay. That'll be 500 yen.

09:56.920 --> 09:58.950
I'm so glad you're still selling them!

10:01.360 --> 10:03.590
I'm a huge fan of Karamitei.

10:03.900 --> 10:06.520
But I wasn't able to make it to the summer Comi-Pa.

10:06.760 --> 10:08.060
For people like you,

10:08.430 --> 10:10.490
here's a drink bonus.

10:10.870 --> 10:12.000
Miss Inagawa!

10:13.700 --> 10:15.430
I'll give you a laminated card as an extra while I'm at it!

10:15.740 --> 10:17.040
Wow!

10:17.810 --> 10:20.940
It's handmade, one-of-a-kind.
Take good care of it.

10:22.910 --> 10:25.210
Since you're at it anyway, can
I ask for an autograph, too?

10:25.620 --> 10:28.210
Man, you know how to work it!

10:28.520 --> 10:31.720
Fine, just for you! Don't tell anyone else!

10:40.900 --> 10:43.700
Here, take a flyer, too.

10:43.970 --> 10:46.100
My group does mail orders, too.

10:46.670 --> 10:47.800
Thank you so much!

10:47.870 --> 10:50.500
I'll be looking forward to the next exhibition and spot sale!

10:51.210 --> 10:53.110
Thanks a bunch! Come again now!

10:53.280 --> 10:54.770
Thank you very much.

10:55.010 --> 10:56.980
That's our first sale of the day.

10:57.280 --> 10:59.180
These are the kinds of exhibition and spot sales...

10:59.180 --> 11:01.050
...where you can really enjoy the heart-to-heart interaction.

11:01.750 --> 11:05.420
<i>It feels good to sell books,</i> <i>even when they're not mine.</i>

11:08.590 --> 11:10.260
Thank you very much!

11:09.190 --> 11:10.730
Thanks a bunch!

11:12.230 --> 11:14.130
Good progress, good progress.

11:15.270 --> 11:17.830
Wanna start doin' lunch in shifts soon?

11:18.000 --> 11:19.330
Yuu, go on ahead.

11:19.440 --> 11:21.410
Okay then, I'll take you at your word.

11:21.540 --> 11:23.870
Hey, there you are!

11:24.310 --> 11:25.140
This voice is...

11:26.340 --> 11:29.710
So, this is where you were!
Hot spring panda cub!

11:30.010 --> 11:31.280
Oh, it's you!

11:41.790 --> 11:44.520
I came because I heard there was a panda selling doujinshi.

11:44.700 --> 11:46.720
I guess the rumor was true.

11:49.600 --> 11:51.730
I've seen this book before!

11:51.800 --> 11:56.140
Where have I seen it?
Let's see... Let's see...

11:56.240 --> 11:58.070
I know! At Comi-Pa!

11:58.140 --> 11:59.740
Don't tell me these are leftovers!

12:00.080 --> 12:03.640
Whoa, talk about uncool! So lame!

12:04.550 --> 12:06.950
Shut yer mouth, Eimi Oh Bad!

12:07.050 --> 12:09.020
My last name is Ohba! Eimi Ohba!

12:09.220 --> 12:10.710
Don't go around changing my name!

12:10.960 --> 12:12.220
What are ya talkin' about?

12:12.220 --> 12:14.490
If I didn't change it, it wouldn't reflect who you really are.

12:14.760 --> 12:15.780
What did you say?!

12:16.160 --> 12:18.190
Shoot, the truth just slipped out.

12:18.430 --> 12:20.660
What?! What?! What?!
You hot spring panda cub!

12:20.730 --> 12:22.100
Panda! Panda! Panda!

12:22.170 --> 12:23.160
Hey, stop this.

12:23.530 --> 12:25.470
I've been wonderin' for a while about this.

12:25.570 --> 12:28.060
Don't you know any words other than "panda"?

12:28.140 --> 12:30.200
Why don't you increase your vocabulary already?

12:30.310 --> 12:31.900
Vo-vocabulary?

12:32.480 --> 12:37.410
Vocabulary. A collection of words used within a certain context.

12:38.280 --> 12:38.910
Thanks.

12:39.650 --> 12:42.210
Make sure you remember that! It might be on a test.

12:42.290 --> 12:46.280
Don't get uppity just because you know some hard words!

12:46.360 --> 12:48.120
I'm not gettin' uppity.

12:48.190 --> 12:51.490
Humph! You don't stand a chance against me!

12:51.930 --> 12:57.270
Because I'm the king of kings among doujinshi authors!

12:57.940 --> 12:59.800
Shouldn't that be "queen of queens"?

13:01.710 --> 13:02.670
Come to think of it, she's right.

13:03.070 --> 13:04.940
Yeah, women can't become kings.

13:05.410 --> 13:07.400
Th-that has nothing to do with this!

13:08.250 --> 13:13.340
Anyway, I, the great, cute Eimi
Ohba, am a lot greater than you!

13:13.750 --> 13:17.690
I've even started writing the book for the winter Comi-Pa already!

13:18.020 --> 13:19.720
Being fast doesn't make you better.

13:19.820 --> 13:21.160
What's important is what's inside.

13:21.230 --> 13:24.290
What's inside is wonderful, too! It's got good content!

13:24.430 --> 13:27.130
You just picked up on the popular elements again anyway, right?

13:27.500 --> 13:31.990
That's not true.
I've arranged it in my own style.

13:32.240 --> 13:34.210
Don't group me in with those other groups...

13:34.310 --> 13:36.870
...that just draw comics based on fads!

13:38.040 --> 13:39.700
My doujinshi will be extremely awesome,

13:39.810 --> 13:41.570
it'll sell out in no time at all,

13:41.650 --> 13:47.050
and I'll bet I'll have more time than I know what to do with at the winter Comi-Pa!

13:47.520 --> 13:48.920
Is that so?

13:48.920 --> 13:52.420
Then you go use that free time to study and increase your vocabulary.

13:52.420 --> 13:54.290
Vocabulary

13:52.920 --> 13:54.290
Your vo-cabu-lary!

13:54.490 --> 13:56.890
Wh-what about my vocabulary?!

13:57.060 --> 14:00.500
Humph! The hot spring panda cub is nothing!

14:00.830 --> 14:02.660
Humph! Humph! Humph!

14:03.600 --> 14:04.860
And humph!

14:05.770 --> 14:07.740
She's the same as ever.

14:08.010 --> 14:10.800
But no matter what I say about her, she's still amazin'.

14:10.940 --> 14:12.070
That Eimi.

14:12.180 --> 14:12.870
What?

14:12.940 --> 14:15.210
She shows up frequently at exhibition and spot sales,

14:15.380 --> 14:17.780
researches the preferences of her customers,

14:17.920 --> 14:20.610
and her comic techniques are top notch to begin with.

14:21.150 --> 14:22.890
No wonder she sells well.

14:22.890 --> 14:25.720
I did research too, though...

14:26.560 --> 14:28.550
But I guess that's not enough.

14:28.760 --> 14:32.320
Just taking in popular elements doesn't make a doujinshi sell.

14:32.600 --> 14:35.620
You shouldn't worry about it. It's over already.

14:36.170 --> 14:38.640
A doujinshi isn't good just because it sells.

14:38.940 --> 14:41.270
Well, sure, there's nothin' wrong if it sells,

14:41.370 --> 14:43.070
but that's not all there is to it.

14:43.240 --> 14:46.540
That's probably what people in every group think.

14:53.580 --> 14:54.810
Um...

14:55.520 --> 14:56.350
Lunch...

14:56.790 --> 15:00.820
Oh, right. I completely forgot 'cause Eimi came along.

15:01.230 --> 15:02.960
Well, I'll be goin' then.

15:03.060 --> 15:04.360
Oh, sure.

15:08.830 --> 15:12.860
I'm sorry for the commotion.
It must have been annoying for you.

15:13.640 --> 15:14.370
Not at all.

15:19.380 --> 15:19.900
Mami Iwasa

15:19.980 --> 15:20.580
Emu Otoku

15:20.580 --> 15:21.180
Hiroko Kurimoto

15:21.180 --> 15:21.550
Norihiko Sudoh

15:21.550 --> 15:23.380
Kazuki Sendou

15:38.630 --> 15:39.900
It's pretty slow.

15:39.900 --> 15:41.090
Yes.

15:43.470 --> 15:44.770
Um...

15:45.270 --> 15:47.740
Don't you have a book of your own?

15:48.170 --> 15:51.470
What? No, I'm just a shopboy today.

15:52.240 --> 15:53.540
I see.

15:55.580 --> 15:56.380
Um...

15:57.080 --> 15:58.450
I read it.

15:59.280 --> 16:02.550
Your book from the summer Comi-Pa.

16:03.050 --> 16:05.050
From Comi-Pa? Oh.

16:10.830 --> 16:13.230
It is a book I could never write.

16:13.230 --> 16:15.530
The People

16:16.170 --> 16:19.030
Um, I quit doing doujin work.

16:19.740 --> 16:22.540
I won't draw anymore comics or create anymore doujinshi.

16:23.540 --> 16:25.030
That's what I decided.

16:26.710 --> 16:30.110
The truth is, that book sold horribly.

16:31.720 --> 16:33.950
I did so much research and drew the comic by pulling all-nighters,

16:33.950 --> 16:35.780
working frantically to put it together.

16:36.920 --> 16:39.360
But all I got for it was exhaustion and a mountain of leftovers.

16:39.490 --> 16:40.960
It's so stupid.

16:42.430 --> 16:44.260
Is it important?

16:44.830 --> 16:46.000
What?

16:46.000 --> 16:50.370
Is being able to sell lots of copies such an important thing?

16:51.500 --> 16:53.160
Isn't it important to you, Miss Aya?

16:55.570 --> 16:59.130
Miss Aya, why do you participate in exhibition and spot sales?

16:59.910 --> 17:02.440
Why do you create doujinshi?

17:04.380 --> 17:05.970
Because it is fun.

17:06.920 --> 17:09.550
Because I like it. Because it is fun.

17:10.020 --> 17:11.350
Fun?

17:11.720 --> 17:14.850
Not much of a yield today, as expected.

17:15.030 --> 17:17.430
There's nothing you can do about it in this season.

17:17.490 --> 17:20.020
But it is irking to go home empty-handed.

17:20.160 --> 17:21.890
What about this area?

17:26.470 --> 17:29.740
It's got the key elements down and quite a bit of originality.

17:29.940 --> 17:31.740
This is a pleasant surprise!

17:32.010 --> 17:33.380
Oh, thank you.

17:33.710 --> 17:35.480
So, how much is it?

17:36.110 --> 17:39.140
This one is 500 yen. That one is 200 yen.

17:39.480 --> 17:41.710
200 yen? How inexpensive.

17:42.620 --> 17:43.680
Very conscientious.

17:44.190 --> 17:47.060
We're having a sale right now.
Please buy some.

17:47.860 --> 17:50.230
Very well. We shall take them.

17:51.160 --> 17:52.930
We pay money.

17:53.030 --> 17:54.120
Thank you.

17:54.200 --> 17:56.190
Thank you very much.

17:56.800 --> 18:00.530
You will have a booth at the winter
Comi-Pa as well, will you not?

18:00.670 --> 18:02.970
Well, probably.

18:04.210 --> 18:06.970
We'll look forward to it.
Keep up the good work.

18:07.440 --> 18:10.180
What? Yes, we will. Thank you.

18:11.620 --> 18:12.880
Bye.

18:14.180 --> 18:17.850
It makes you sort of happy when people say they'll look forward to it.

18:20.090 --> 18:22.360
<i>But it's weird, when you think about it.</i>

18:22.660 --> 18:26.930
<i>I'm only selling Yuu's doujinshi,</i> <i>so why am I feeling happy?</i>

18:28.100 --> 18:30.730
<i>Is this what the "fun"is about?</i>

18:31.270 --> 18:33.000
Yo, thanks for waitin'.

18:39.610 --> 18:43.280
<i>If people buy and enjoy the</i> <i>doujinshi you worked so hard on,</i>

18:43.280 --> 18:45.110
<i>I bet you'd feel happy and it'd be fun.</i>

18:46.180 --> 18:47.380
<i>Which means...</i>

18:47.450 --> 18:50.490
<i>I guess an exhibition and spot</i> <i>sale might be sort of a place...</i>

18:50.490 --> 18:53.290
<i>... where the buyers and sellers</i> <i>can meet heart-to-heart.</i>

18:54.060 --> 18:55.460
<i>In that case...</i>

18:55.690 --> 19:00.100
<i>Doujinshi is just a tool for</i> <i>people to meet heart-to-heart.</i>

19:00.530 --> 19:02.590
<i>Maybe it's just an excuse.</i>

19:04.030 --> 19:07.270
<i>Thank you very much for coming today.</i>

19:08.010 --> 19:13.000
<i>We will now be bringing</i>
<i>Comic Wasshoi to a close.</i>

19:25.960 --> 19:26.950
Um...

19:27.990 --> 19:30.150
Thank you very much for today.

19:30.930 --> 19:33.420
Thanks a bunch, you were a great help, too.

19:33.500 --> 19:34.900
Take care.

19:35.300 --> 19:36.560
I will.

19:38.400 --> 19:40.100
At another exhibition and spot sale, then.

19:40.570 --> 19:41.770
What?

19:45.680 --> 19:48.580
Now we're done here, too. Shall we go home?

19:48.980 --> 19:49.810
Sure.

19:49.810 --> 19:51.750
Well? Do you feel a little better now?

19:53.250 --> 19:55.120
You talked to all sorts of people,

19:55.190 --> 19:57.650
so it probably distracted you for a while, right?

19:57.720 --> 19:58.960
I suppose so.

19:58.960 --> 20:02.720
<i>Wait, Yuu could've handled today's</i> <i>exhibition and spot sale alone...</i>

20:03.230 --> 20:06.160
Participatin' is what makes exhibition and spot sales meaningful.

20:06.460 --> 20:07.950
You understand now, right?

20:09.770 --> 20:10.730
Yuu.

20:10.800 --> 20:11.860
What?

20:12.100 --> 20:13.070
Thank you.

20:13.140 --> 20:13.970
What?!

20:13.970 --> 20:18.710
D-don't get so serious all of a sudden! You're scarin' me!

20:19.080 --> 20:20.480
Oh, sorry.

20:21.980 --> 20:23.280
Oh, right.

20:24.450 --> 20:25.510
Here.

20:30.190 --> 20:31.750
I bought them when I had some time.

20:31.820 --> 20:34.380
They're all doujinshi within your field of ability.

20:34.460 --> 20:35.980
Use them for reference.

20:36.090 --> 20:37.390
But I...

20:37.530 --> 20:38.830
It's your pay as a shopboy!

20:39.560 --> 20:41.360
Don't say anythin' and just take them.

20:41.700 --> 20:44.360
They're...well, my feelings.

20:48.170 --> 20:51.670
Comrade Kazuki! It seems you have finally begun to grasp the concept.

20:52.180 --> 20:55.200
I believe in you and I am waiting!

20:55.510 --> 20:57.780
There will come a day when you will rise again.

20:58.650 --> 21:02.480
And that day will become the day we truly begin conquering the world!

21:06.460 --> 21:08.790
To: Hokkaido

21:48.670 --> 21:50.460
Doujin work...

22:19.860 --> 22:24.100
<i>The distant sky looked bright...</i>
<i>Touku no Sora ga Akaruku Mieta</i>

22:24.100 --> 22:28.560
<i>...and we began walking.</i>
<i>Soshite Bokura wa Arukihajimeta</i>

22:28.710 --> 22:33.110
<i>Getting our feet caught in the mud.</i>
<i>Nukarumi ni Ashi o Torarenagara</i>

22:33.280 --> 22:37.180
<i>Heading for a shapeless city.</i>
<i>Katachi no Nai Machi o Mezashite</i>

22:37.180 --> 22:41.290
<i>The pocket in my heart was full...</i>
<i>Kokoro no Naka no Pocket ni wa</i>

22:41.290 --> 22:45.550
<i>...of the grownup things we'd just learned.</i>
<i>Oboetate no Otona ga Ippai</i>

22:45.720 --> 22:50.160
<i>Having taken off our uniforms...</i>
<i>Seifuku o Nuida Bokura ni wa</i>

22:50.290 --> 22:54.300
<i>... the wind was just a little too cold.</i>
<i>Kaze wa Sukoshi Tsumetasugita</i>

22:54.300 --> 22:57.870
<i>Who in the world am I?</i>
<i>Ittai Boku wa Dare Darou</i>

22:57.870 --> 23:02.770
<i>I think about that every so often.</i>
<i>Tokidoki Sonna Koto o Omou</i>

23:02.940 --> 23:06.440
<i>In the world outside the school building...</i>
<i>Kousha no Soto no Sekai de wa</i>

23:06.440 --> 23:11.850
<i>...it's like everyone is a</i> <i>pawn in a game of chess.</i>
<i>Daremo ga Marude Chess no Koma sa</i>

23:12.950 --> 23:17.390
<i>I'm here for you.</i>
<i>Kimi no Tame ni Boku ga Ite</i>

23:17.390 --> 23:21.390
<i>And you for me.</i>
<i>Boku no Tame ni Kimiga</i>

23:21.390 --> 23:25.930
<i>When you think about that...</i>
<i>Sou Omoeba Daremo ga</i>

23:25.930 --> 23:34.900
<i>... everyone is needed by someone.</i>
<i>Dareka no Tame ni Hitsuyou sa</i>

23:55.530 --> 24:19.880
PREVIEW

23:59.760 --> 24:01.370
You know, Kazuki?

24:01.370 --> 24:02.670
What?

24:01.970 --> 24:04.770
Um, well, that is...

24:05.070 --> 24:06.400
What is it, Mizuki?

24:06.400 --> 24:10.940
That is, so...
How should I say this? Well...

24:11.210 --> 24:13.610
So, what is it you're trying to say?

24:13.610 --> 24:17.050
Oh, I can't say it out loud, so just watch this!

24:17.650 --> 24:19.650
Next time, "The Distance Between Them."

24:19.880 --> 24:22.390
Don't miss it, okay? You gotta promise!

24:20.380 --> 24:26.150
NEXT TIME

24:20.380 --> 24:26.150
THE DISTANCE

24:20.380 --> 24:26.150
BETWEEN THEM

24:22.650 --> 24:24.390
Uh, okay, got it.
